<row>
  <text>
    ## Alignment inside a column

    By default this deck centers the two columns vertically (`columns` in `deck.json`). Here the code is pinned to the
    top of its column with `valign=start` on the `<code>`; a slide can do the same for everything with `valign: start`.
  </text>
  <code lang=rust id=g1 valign=start>
    <frame>
      fn main() {
          let name = "slides";
          println!("hello, {name}");
      }
    </frame>
    <frame>
      fn main() {
          let name = "slides";
          let count = 3;
          for i in 0..count {
              println!("{i}: hello, {name}");
          }
      }
    </frame>
  </code>
</row>
